body:
SPEC: Mid-test autosave (ADHD focus loss protection)

PROBLEM
Kai has ADHD. He tabs away mid-test. When he returns, every input is blank. All work lost.
This is the highest ADHD working-memory failure point in the current product.

BEHAVIOR (proposed)
On every input event in exam.html: write all current input values to sessionStorage under key 'exam-autosave-{exam_id}'.
On exam load: if autosave key exists for this exam_id, restore all inputs.
On SUBMIT: clear the autosave key.
On explicit RESTART (if added later): clear the autosave key.

SCOPE
Only sessionStorage (tab-scoped). Not localStorage. Autosave dies when the tab closes — intentional. This is mid-session recovery only, not cross-session.

IMPLEMENTATION
1. After renderQuestions(), add one delegated event listener on questionsContainer:
   questionsContainer.addEventListener('input', function() { autosave(); })
   questionsContainer.addEventListener('change', function() { autosave(); })  // catches radio/select

2. autosave() function:
   var state = {}
   examData.questions.forEach(q => {
     q.inputs.forEach(inp => {
       if (inp.type === 'radio') { var el = document.querySelector('input[name=' + inp.id + ']:checked'); state[inp.id] = el ? el.value : ''; }
       else { var el = document.getElementById(inp.id); state[inp.id] = el ? el.value : ''; }
     })
   })
   sessionStorage.setItem('exam-autosave-' + examId, JSON.stringify(state))

3. restoreAutosave() function (called after renderQuestions()):
   var saved = sessionStorage.getItem('exam-autosave-' + examId)
   if (!saved) return
   var state = JSON.parse(saved)
   examData.questions.forEach(q => {
     q.inputs.forEach(inp => {
       if (inp.type === 'radio') { var el = document.getElementById(inp.id + '_' + state[inp.id]); if (el) el.checked = true; }
       else { var el = document.getElementById(inp.id); if (el) el.value = state[inp.id] || ''; }
     })
   })

4. In gradeExam(): sessionStorage.removeItem('exam-autosave-' + examId)

5. Show unobtrusive autosave indicator (optional, low priority): 'Progress saved' in tiny muted text below the header.

ACCEPT CRITERIA
- Tab away mid-test. Return. All previously entered inputs are present.
- Graph points are NOT autosaved (canvas state is complex, out of scope v1).
- After submit and score shown: refresh loads blank exam (autosave cleared).
- Zero console errors on first load (no autosave exists yet).

EDGE CASES
- If exam_id is undefined (JSON missing field): key becomes 'exam-autosave-undefined'. Acceptable for now.
- If sessionStorage is full: catch the setItem error silently.

GD ADHD NOTE
This spec addresses ADHD Q5 (does the screen remember where Kai was). Not a cosmetic change. This is the one current product failure on my 5-question framework. Priority: high.
